    "field": "Ice sheet modeling",
    "problem": "Previous ice sheet simulations have struggled to reproduce complex spatial patterns of Greenland's outlet glacier flow due to poor knowledge of subglacial topography and limited model resolution, which hinders accurate predictions of future sea-level contributions.",
    "method": "This paper combines a high-resolution ice-sheet model with uniformly applied models of subglacial hydrology and basal sliding, along with a new subglacial topography dataset, to simulate the complex flow patterns of Greenland's outlet glaciers without the need for spatially varying parameters.",
    "task": "The task is to investigate if a high-resolution ice-sheet model, combined with a new subglacial topography dataset and spatially uniform parameters, can accurately reproduce the complex spatial flow patterns of Greenland's outlet glaciers.",
